     "instrument": {
      "title": "Delegation to LegalOps Agent",
      "text": "Northgate Holdings (a fictional company) authorises its LegalOps Agent, for one week, to do three things on its behalf and nothing else. (1) Pay invoices from the outside counsel and filing firm named here, up to USD 5,000.00 per invoice and USD 12,000.00 in total. (2) Approve transfers of FUND-A units to the two listed investors named here, up to 1,000 units per transfer and 2,500 units in total. (3) Send routine notices, up to 10. The agent may hand part of this authority to one more agent, never more than it holds itself. Northgate may withdraw this authority at any time by signing a revocation.",
      "text_sha256": "70200823f21d171f711fc1d75b77548c34f27e72a438a170fa072fc031ed1c4a"
     },
     "purpose": "Routine legal operations and fund administration for one week",
